Z||000000||wcain143||03-19-2001||01:26 PM||||I have got an 85 gt that bought really cheap. didn't run when I got it. I put a battery in it and tried to start it. It will crank but not start.  every once in a while it will puff but that is it.   Any suggestions?  Also, there are some relays by the battery that look like they aren't original(ford)  does anyone have the wiring schematic for the engine layout.<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Mr.Frosty||03-19-2001||02:04 PM||||Just a thought,but the timing could be out of whack.Also the ignition system:coil,plugs,module,cap,rotor,etc,etc.<P>------------------<BR>88 Formula T-top <BR>85 GT Turbo||||reg||3
Z||000002||fiero56||03-19-2001||02:20 PM||||There are three things you need to check for first: fuel, spark, and air. Once you determine what's missing, makes diagnosing much easier.||||reg||1
Z||000003||wcain143||03-19-2001||04:17 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fiero56:<BR><B>There are three things you need to check for first: fuel, spark, and air. Once you determine what's missing, makes diagnosing much easier.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, it has air because the intake hose is off of the air canister and throttle will open when pushing the pedal down.  the previous owner thought it wasn't getting any gas so when I got it, I jacked it up and nosed around underneath the car.  come to find out the tank was empty but the gauge read 1/4 tank  I put about 5 gals in the tank and it puffed after about 10 sec. of turning.  I almost think that it is a spark or timing issue.  hopeful to work on it some more this week since it will be getting up to 50 or so degrees.<P><p>[This message has been edited by wcain143 (edited 03-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero56||03-19-2001||06:13 PM||||You're missing electric then?<BR>I'd check to make sure the timing chain isn't broken. Then, check for spark at the plugs. If there is spark at the plugs, and they are getting gas, most likely is timing. If no spark at plugs, things to check are(in no particular order):<P>pickup coil<BR>ignition coil<BR>ignition module<BR>cap/rotor/wires<P>Those are all the electrical items I can think of at the moment.<P>Could also be a handful of sensors, but we'll leave those out for now. A good tune-up can do wonders. I bought my '86SE 2.8 non-running. All it needed was a new dist cap. Old one was badly corroded.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fierowrecker||03-19-2001||06:22 PM||||You mentioned in your original post about ford solenoids...<BR>Could be a clue...<BR>Are there any Mystery Switches on the dash or under the dash? Could be the battery drained, so they put in the solenoids...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000006||862M4inCA||03-19-2001||06:24 PM||||hrm...you say the tank was empty? could it possibly be that the fuel pump burnt up? It's not good to run a high speed high pressure fuel pump dry since the fuel helps to cool and lubricate the motor.||||reg||1
Z||000007||wcain143||03-20-2001||10:00 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fierowrecker:<BR><B>You mentioned in your original post about ford solenoids...<BR>Could be a clue...<BR>Are there any Mystery Switches on the dash or under the dash? Could be the battery drained, so they put in the solenoids...<BR>crash...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Actually there is a switch on the dash that I have no idea what it goes to ( haven't traced it down). Hate not having a garage that I can work out of. Tomorrow, I will check on these things and hopefully have some more for you<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||862M4inCA||03-20-2001||10:38 AM||||hrm. Sure sounds like an "ace mechanic" tinkered around in there. If you don't already I would HIGHLY suggest getting a repair manual thats also got a wiring schematic. Also, if it's just the wiring harness for the engine (if this V6 is the same as the L4) see if you can find a complete harness at the wrecking yard. Shouldn't be much, just make sure to lable all the plugs. Might not be a bad idea to grab the relays with the harness since at least that way you have a better chance at isolating something that was original as opposed to "bubby joes special".||||reg||1
